meta {
  name: 1a List providers — clamp probe
  type: http
  seq: 2
}
get {
  url: {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/providers?page=1&pageSize=100000
}
params:query {
  page: 1
  pageSize: 100000
}
tests {
  test("clamped to 100 and echoed, NOT a 400", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
    // F-020-T11: wrapped in DataResponse<T> -- the pageSize moved under "data".
    expect(res.getBody().data.pageSize).to.equal(100);
  });
}
docs {
  Deliberate probe of the security control. Rejecting with `400` would tell an attacker the exact
  boundary and leave an honest client no way to discover the cap; clamping and echoing the effective
  value lets a well-behaved client detect it and paginate correctly.
}
